{
  "approved": false,
  "comments": [
    "No changes were made to src/shorten_route.py to add URL validation; the implementation still lacks the required helper and error handling.",
    "tests/test_app.py was not updated or extended with the new validation tests described in the spec, so the test coverage for missing body, missing url field, empty string, non‑string, malformed URL, and valid URL cases is absent.",
    "Edge cases such as non‑JSON payloads, missing Content-Type, URLs without scheme/netloc, whitespace‑only strings, and extremely long URLs are not addressed in code.",
    "Error responses currently do not return the JSON structure ('error' key) expected by the spec, and status codes may be incorrect.",
    "Add the _is_valid_url helper, update the POST handler to perform all required checks, and create the six test cases to verify proper 400 responses and a successful 201 response."
  ]
}
